Ex) Rule 21 (primitive type variable should not be zero)
    {v_1 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≠ 0

[Example Rules]
Rule 26 (tuple of ints used as kernel size must have length 2)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] > 0

Rule 12 (a primitive type variable is smaller than the other)
{v_1 : int ⊎ float, v_2 : int ⊎ float} |= v_1 ≤ v_2

Rule 13 (tensor must have a floating-point dtype: 6–8)
{v1: tensor} |= 6 ≤ dtype(v1) ∧ dtype(v1) ≤ 8

